    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A small Christian kingdom in the Cantabrian Mountains founded after the Muslim conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, traditionally at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-covadonga">Covadonga</a>.</li><li>Its kings claimed to restore the Visigothic order, an idea that later fed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a>.</li><li>Expansion to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douro">Douro</a> shifted power south, and in 924 the kingdom merged into the Kingdom of León.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pelagius-of-asturias">Pelagius</a>’s son and successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/favila-of-asturias">Favila</a> was killed by a bear in 739, after only two years as king, according to the Asturian chronicles.</p></aside>
    </section>

